<title>USA: TIN--ATPC dead, put the cash into promotion -trade.</title>
<headline>TIN--ATPC dead, put the cash into promotion -trade.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Association of Tin Producing Countries (ATPC) is as good as dead and spare cash in the industry should be funnelled into promoting the metal, U.S. traders and producer agents said.</p>
<p>&quot;The ATPC is a dead old duck. It's history,&quot; said a tin trading and producer executive. &quot;We have ITRI, that's where any money should go,&quot; he added, referring to the International Tin Research Institute.</p>
<p>ATPC, which used to set quotas on exports, is due to meet in Singapore on September 23-24.</p>
</text>
